     "Distance-users,\r<br>\r<br>I have point transect data with landscape parameters around each point\r<br>count stop and I used Distance to find the best-fitting detection model.\r<br> This top model has the covariate &quot;%grass in a 100-m radius buffer\r<br>around each point&quot;.  I would now like to fit a model that best predicts\r<br>per point density (I already have those estimates) using the same\r<br>landscape variables used to build the detection model.  Does distance\r<br>perform this analysis or, and this would make me feel really dumb, does\r<br>the best detection model =  best density model?\r<br>\r<br>Many thanks,\r<br>\r<br>Jeff\r<br>\r<br>****************************************\r<br>Jeff Stratford\r<br>331 Funchess Hall\r<br>Department of Biological Sciences\r<br>Auburn University\r<br>Auburn, AL 36849\r<br>FAX <a href=\"tel:(334)%20844-9234\" value=\"+13348449234\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">334-844-9234</a>\r<br><a href=\"http://www.auburn.edu/~stratja\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.auburn.edu/~stratja&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792479545956000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2XicmK6ELpPYPbyf15Xgig\">http://www.auburn.edu/~stratja</a>\r<br>****************************************\r<br>"
